  "kind": "bit-matching-detail",
  "title": "PV takes the linear branch only at exact rate == 0 and stores x87 (1 + rate) before POWER and annuity discounting",
  "statement": "In Excel 16.0.20131 through 16.0.20527, PV(rate, nper, pmt, [fv], [type]) takes the linear route -(fv + pmt * nper) only when rate == 0.0 exactly. For nonzero rate it forms base = RN53(RN64(1 + rate)), computes factor = POWER(base, nper) (returning #DIV/0! when factor == 0), forms term = RN53(RN64(RN53(RN64((factor - 1) / rate)) * timing)), and evaluates -RN53(RN64(RN53(RN64(fv + RN53(RN64(pmt * term)))) / factor)). All 1,564 full-bank PV rows match.",
  "status": "measured",
  "basis": "Measured across Excel 16.0.20131, 20430, and 20527.20088, matching 1,564/1,564 full-bank and 120/120 pinned PV rows.",
